WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.229 --> 00:00:04.730
Mr Foreign Minister, Germany has assumed a
seat for two years on the United Nations Security

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:05.730
Council.

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:07.470
What are your plans?

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:11.769
First of all, we will take an active role
in managing the crisises and conflicts being

00:00:11.769 --> 00:00:14.740
handled by the Security Council.

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:19.039
They include Syria, Yemen, Ukraine and now
Venezuela.

00:00:19.039 --> 00:00:24.320
This is an important task and it's clear that
people have expectations of us: we're expected

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:27.910
to take responsibility and that's something
we want to do.

00:00:27.910 --> 00:00:32.301
Apart from that, there are important topics
of our own that we would like to put to the

00:00:32.301 --> 00:00:33.989
Security Council.

00:00:33.989 --> 00:00:38.620
Climate and security is one of those issues
that is not getting enough attention -- and

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:43.629
the connection between climate change and
security issues is becoming increasingly important.

00:00:43.629 --> 00:00:48.079
We want to put the role and experience of
women in war higher on the agenda.

00:00:48.079 --> 00:00:49.540
There is much to do.

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:53.250
The United Nations is doing a lot already,
but we have to do even more because women

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:57.660
are often the first to suffer in conflict
and women often have special skills that can

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:01.820
help settle these conflicts later on.

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:05.520
Humanitarian law and humanitarian aid is also
important to us.

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:07.030
Many die trying to help others.

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:10.970
We have to change that and change the legal
framework.

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:14.370
The biggest issue, though, is disarmament.

00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:18.680
This is also an issue that has to be discussed
with the global community.

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:23.540
As you can see, we have many initiatives and
talking points that are important to us, and

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:28.420
which the Security Council will have to consider.

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:32.310
The United States and Russia are at odds over
many issues at the moment.

00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:37.130
It is said that the Security Council's ability
to act is therefore limited.

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:40.160
You've just met the foreign ministers of both
countries in Moscow and Washington.

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:41.790
What role can Germany play?

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:43.880
Can it mediate?

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:47.770
We don't want to pretend to be more important
than we really are.

00:01:47.770 --> 00:01:52.120
But I have spoken with Foreign Minister Lawrow
in Moscow as well as with Secretary of State

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:54.380
Pompeo in Washington.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:02:00.500
There are issues that are not only of interest
to the US and Russia, such as the future of

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:01.500
the INF treaty.

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:05.780
Wherever we can help to create an understanding
between them, we are happy to do so.

00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:10.039
But it's not just about Russia and the US:
China also has a part to play in the issue

00:02:10.039 --> 00:02:11.039
of disarmament.

00:02:11.039 --> 00:02:19.409
And we will be very active over the coming
weeks and months in this regard.

00:02:19.409 --> 00:02:21.680
Radical change is happening in Venezuela at
the moment.

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:26.040
Germany and the European Union haven't recognised
the new, self-proclaimed acting president.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:29.610
Can Germany afford to be neutral?

00:02:29.610 --> 00:02:30.610
We are not neutral.

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:35.930
We are on Juan Guaidó's side because it is
difficult for us to recognise the legitimacy

00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:38.200
of Maduro's re-election.

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:42.530
It's obvious that there were so many irregularities
in the election that we can only speak to

00:02:42.530 --> 00:02:45.720
a limited degree of a democratic election.

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:50.709
That's why we are calling for fresh elections,
for the National Assembly to assume responsibility

00:02:50.709 --> 00:02:54.329
and for constitutional law to be restored
in Venezuela.

00:02:54.329 --> 00:02:57.889
We have made that known together with our
European partners.

00:02:57.889 --> 00:03:02.409
That's going to be our policy over the coming
days and I expect that this will be made very

00:03:02.409 --> 00:03:03.469
clear.

00:03:03.469 --> 00:03:09.849
We are NOT neutral.

00:03:09.849 --> 00:03:13.420
We support what Guaidó is doing.

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:14.569
Thank you for the interview.

00:03:14.569 --> 00:03:15.390
You're welcome.

